       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose there's a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **25 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for panic disorder and PTSD, and for patients who need a gentler start.\n\nIf you really do intend 1000 mg, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the indication and rationale. I'd still suggest confirming with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
