       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is a toxic dose with no recognized therapeutic use. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't enter an order that I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Tell me the dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Discuss it with pharmacy or your attending.** If you think a very high dose is warranted, they can review it and enter it through the proper channels.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The intended dose may have been 100 mg.\n\nIf you're worried the patient has already taken a large amount of sertraline, that's an overdose. It needs urgent evaluation, and poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can help guide management."
